{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 55, :comments ["<b>Thorns.</b> Sharp thorns, from the root of הסר מסוכתו. הנני סך את דרכך בסירים." "<b>And as thorns.</b> Its meaning in context is like 'and to range alongside you' (וּלְשׁוֹטֵט בְּצַדִּיכֶם) — they are blows with a whip, or sharp thorns like צנים פחים. And there is yet another interpretation for them: the border of their inheritance, which they are obligated to dispossess from there the inhabitants of the land."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites two biblical forms from the root סוך/סכך: הסר מסוכתו and הנני סך את דרכך בסירים (Ezekiel 24:6–7). Left in Hebrew script per discipline; the lexicographic argument hinges on the Hebrew forms."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:18.352478241Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}